{"name":"Harpoon","hex":"#283b4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"harpoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, spearlike implement with a barbed head, attached to a line and used to catch and haul in large marine animals such as whales and other cetaceans, seals, walruses, sharks, etc.\nSuch an implement armed with explosives in the head, used to strike and fatally wound cetaceans when whaling.","Such an implement armed with explosives in the head, used to strike and fatally wound cetaceans when whaling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shoot something with a harpoon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harpoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harpoon","blocks":[{"text":"A harpoon is a long, spear-like projectile used in fishing, whaling, sealing, and other hunting to shoot, kill, and capture large fish such as sharks or marine mammals such as seals, sea cows, and whales. It impales the target and secures it with barb or toggling claws, allowing the fishermen or hunters to use an attached rope or chain to pull and retrieve the animal. A harpoon can also be used as a weapon against watercraft in naval warfare."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Inuit_hunter_with_harpoon.jpg/330px-Inuit_hunter_with_harpoon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpoon","wikidata":"Q207574"},{"title":"Harpoon (missile)","blocks":[{"text":"The Harpoon is an all-weather, over-the-horizon, anti-ship missile \nmanufactured by McDonnell Douglas. The AGM-84E Standoff Land Attack Missile (SLAM) and later AGM-84H/K SLAM-ER are cruise missile variants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Harpoon_asm_bowfin_museum.jpg/330px-Harpoon_asm_bowfin_museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpoon_(missile)","wikidata":"Q331436"}],"images":